-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, ea3: PART 15A, ADMINISTRATIVE PENALTIES (ss 126A to 126D;
-- lines 5011-5226 of EmA1968.txt).
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online
-- (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every `-- src:` line copies a line of that file.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the
-- Act does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ea3)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THE SEAMS.  Section 126A asks four provisions of Part 6 of the Act (ea2) whether the employer failed to comply:
-- `the answer of s 95(1)`, `the answer of s 95A(2)`, `the answer of s 96(1)` and `the answer of s 96A` (PLAN.md S9 to S12),
-- each a MAYBE BOOLEAN meaning "the employer failed to comply".  Section 126A answers the keel's
-- `s 2(1) "civil contravention" the contravention is one`, which takes `section 126A declares the contravention to be a civil contravention`.
-- The prescribed amount of an administrative penalty, and the prescribed periods of s 126C, are in regulations that
-- are not among the sources: they are inputs.

§ `Part 15A -- Administrative penalties`

§§ `s 126A Civil contraventions`

-- src:5017 | 126A. The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- src:5018 | contraventions for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:5020 | (a) a failure by an employer to comply with section 95(1),
-- src:5021 | 95A(2) or 96(1);
@ref s 126A(a) (src:5017-5021)
GIVEN `the answer of s 95(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 95A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 96(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126A(a) the failure is a civil contravention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 95(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 95A(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 96(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure by an employer to comply with section 95(1), 95A(2) or 96(1)" declares a failure, and an employer who complied with all three has failed in none
        IF `the answer of s 95(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer of s 95A(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer of s 96(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one of the three answers is not given and none of the others is a failure
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5017 | 126A. The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- src:5018 | contraventions for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:5023 | (aa) a failure, by an employer to whom a notification under
-- src:5024 | section 96A applies, to comply with any requirement in the
-- src:5025 | notification concerning the furnishing to the
-- src:5026 | Commissioner of information on the retrenchment of any
-- src:5027 | employee by the employer;
@ref s 126A(aa) (src:5017-5027)
GIVEN `the answer of s 96A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126A(aa) the failure is a civil contravention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 96A`
    WHEN JUST failed THEN
        IF failed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure, by an employer to whom a notification under section 96A applies, to comply with any requirement in the notification"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the employer failed to comply with the notification is the answer of section 96A and the notification
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:5017 | 126A. The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- src:5018 | contraventions for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:5029 | (ab) a contravention, by an employer of any provision of any
-- src:5030 | regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa), that the
-- src:5031 | Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) as a
-- src:5032 | contravention to which this section applies;
@ref s 126A(ab) (src:5017-5032)
GIVEN `the contravention is by an employer of a provision of regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) the contravention as one to which section 126A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126A(ab) the contravention is a civil contravention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contravention is by an employer of a provision of regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa)` AND `the Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) the contravention as one to which section 126A applies` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 2(1) "civil contravention" "means a contravention that is declared to be a civil contravention under section 126A", and paragraph (ab) declares only a contravention of a provision of the regulations that "the Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) as a contravention to which this section applies" (ruling (a) on delegated definitions, 2026-11-05)
        IF `the contravention is by an employer of a provision of regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which contraventions the Minister has prescribed is in regulations that are not among the sources; a contravention that is not of a provision of those regulations is not the subject of paragraph (ab)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5017 | 126A. The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- src:5018 | contraventions for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:5034 | (b) provision by an employer of inaccurate information or
-- src:5035 | particulars to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer
-- src:5040 | under this Act, inadvertently or without intent to mislead or
-- src:5041 | defraud.
@ref s 126A(b) (src:5017-5041)
GIVEN `the employer provided inaccurate information or particulars to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer did so inadvertently or without intent to mislead or defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126A(b) the provision of information is a civil contravention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employer provided inaccurate information or particulars to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer under this Act` AND `the employer did so inadvertently or without intent to mislead or defraud` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 2(1) "civil contravention" "means a contravention that is declared to be a civil contravention under section 126A", and paragraph (b) declares only inaccurate information given "inadvertently or without intent to mislead or defraud"; inaccurate information given with intent to mislead or defraud is not declared (ruling (a) on delegated definitions, 2026-11-05)
        IF `the employer provided inaccurate information or particulars to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer under this Act` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) is about inaccurate information or particulars; a provision of information that is not inaccurate is not its subject
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 126A Kind of contravention` IS ONE OF
    `s 126A(a) a failure by an employer to comply with section 95(1), 95A(2) or 96(1)`
    `s 126A(aa) a failure by an employer to whom a notification under section 96A applies to comply with a requirement in it`
    `s 126A(ab) a contravention by an employer of a provision of regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa)`
    `s 126A(b) the provision by an employer of inaccurate information or particulars, inadvertently or without intent to mislead or defraud`
    `s 126A a contravention of some other kind`

-- src:5017 | 126A. The following contraventions are declared to be civil
-- src:5018 | contraventions for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:5020 | (a) a failure by an employer to comply with section 95(1),
-- src:5021 | 95A(2) or 96(1);
-- src:5023 | (aa) a failure, by an employer to whom a notification under
-- src:5024 | section 96A applies, to comply with any requirement in the
-- src:5025 | notification concerning the furnishing to the
-- src:5026 | Commissioner of information on the retrenchment of any
-- src:5027 | employee by the employer;
-- src:5029 | (ab) a contravention, by an employer of any provision of any
-- src:5030 | regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa), that the
-- src:5031 | Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) as a
-- src:5032 | contravention to which this section applies;
-- src:5034 | (b) provision by an employer of inaccurate information or
-- src:5035 | particulars to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer
-- src:5040 | under this Act, inadvertently or without intent to mislead or
-- src:5041 | defraud.
@ref s 126A (src:5017-5041)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 126A Kind of contravention`
      `the answer of s 126A(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 126A(aa)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 126A(ab)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 126A(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126A the contravention is declared to be a civil contravention` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 126A(a) a failure by an employer to comply with section 95(1), 95A(2) or 96(1)` THEN `the answer of s 126A(a)`
    WHEN `s 126A(aa) a failure by an employer to whom a notification under section 96A applies to comply with a requirement in it` THEN `the answer of s 126A(aa)`
    WHEN `s 126A(ab) a contravention by an employer of a provision of regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa)` THEN `the answer of s 126A(ab)`
    WHEN `s 126A(b) the provision by an employer of inaccurate information or particulars, inadvertently or without intent to mislead or defraud` THEN `the answer of s 126A(b)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following contraventions are declared to be civil contraventions for the purposes of this Act" names four, and "civil contravention" in section 2(1) means a contravention declared under section 126A (src:384-385) (fork F10)
    WHEN `s 126A a contravention of some other kind` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `s 126B Payment of administrative penalty`

-- src:5047 | 126B.—(1) An authorised officer may issue a contravention notice
-- src:5048 | to an employer requiring the employer to pay an administrative
-- src:5049 | penalty of the prescribed amount, for —
-- src:5051 | (a) each occasion of an alleged failure by the employer to
-- src:5052 | comply with section 95(1), 95A(2) or 96(1) with respect to
-- src:5053 | any one employee or former employee;
-- src:5055 | (aa) each occasion of an alleged failure by the employer to
-- src:5056 | comply with any requirement, in a notification under
-- src:5057 | section 96A that applies to the employer, concerning the
-- src:5058 | furnishing to the Commissioner of information on the
-- src:5059 | retrenchment of any one employee by the employer;
-- src:5061 | (ab) each occasion of an alleged contravention, of any provision
-- src:5062 | of any regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa), that
-- src:5063 | the Minister has prescribed under section 139(2B) as a
-- src:5064 | contravention to which section 126A applies, by the
-- src:5065 | employer; or
-- src:5067 | (b) each occasion of an alleged provision by the employer of
-- src:5068 | inaccurate information or particulars to the Commissioner
-- src:5069 | or an inspecting officer under this Act, inadvertently or
-- src:5070 | without intent to mislead or defraud.
@ref s 126B(1) (src:5047-5070)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occasion is an alleged failure or contravention of the kind in paragraph (a), (aa), (ab) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126B(1) the authorised officer may issue a contravention notice to the employer for the occasion` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authorised officer` AND `the occasion is an alleged failure or contravention of the kind in paragraph (a), (aa), (ab) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an authorised officer, for each occasion of an alleged failure or contravention of the four kinds
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5047 | 126B.—(1) An authorised officer may issue a contravention notice
-- src:5048 | to an employer requiring the employer to pay an administrative
-- src:5049 | penalty of the prescribed amount, for —
-- src:5089 | (3) Different amounts of administrative penalty may be prescribed
-- src:5090 | for different civil contraventions or different circumstances in which
-- src:5091 | a civil contravention takes place.
@ref s 126B(1) (src:5047-5091)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed for the occasion` IS A NUMBER
      `the occasion is a second or subsequent occasion of the civil contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 126B(1) the administrative penalty the notice may require` MEANS
    IF `the amount prescribed for the occasion` AT MOST (`s 139(2)(h) the greatest administrative penalty the regulations may prescribe for the occasion` `the occasion is a second or subsequent occasion of the civil contravention`)
    THEN JUST `the amount prescribed for the occasion`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount is "the prescribed amount" of regulations that are not among the sources, and section 139(2)(h) allows no amount above $1,000 for an occasion, or $2,000 for a second or subsequent occasion
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraphs (a) and (aa) count each occasion "with respect to any one employee": the occasions are counted employee by employee.
-- src:5047 | 126B.—(1) An authorised officer may issue a contravention notice
-- src:5048 | to an employer requiring the employer to pay an administrative
-- src:5049 | penalty of the prescribed amount, for —
-- src:5051 | (a) each occasion of an alleged failure by the employer to
-- src:5052 | comply with section 95(1), 95A(2) or 96(1) with respect to
-- src:5053 | any one employee or former employee;
-- src:5055 | (aa) each occasion of an alleged failure by the employer to
-- src:5056 | comply with any requirement, in a notification under
-- src:5057 | section 96A that applies to the employer, concerning the
-- src:5058 | furnishing to the Commissioner of information on the
-- src:5059 | retrenchment of any one employee by the employer;
-- src:5061 | (ab) each occasion of an alleged contravention, of any provision
-- src:5062 | of any regulations mentioned in section 139(2)(aa), that
@ref s 126B(1) (src:5047-5062)
GIVEN `the number of occasions of the alleged failure with respect to each employee or former employee` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 126B(1)(a) and (aa) the number of occasions for which a notice may require an administrative penalty` MEANS
    sum `the number of occasions of the alleged failure with respect to each employee or former employee`

-- src:5074 | (2) A contravention notice must —
-- src:5076 | (a) specify the amount of administrative penalty to be paid;
-- src:5078 | (b) specify the date by which the administrative penalty must
-- src:5079 | be paid; and
-- src:5081 | (c) set out the brief details of the alleged contravention and
-- src:5082 | such other particulars as may be prescribed.
@ref s 126B(2) (src:5074-5082)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the amount of administrative penalty to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the date by which the administrative penalty must be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice sets out the brief details of the alleged contravention and such other particulars as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126B(2) the contravention notice is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the amount of administrative penalty to be paid` AND `the notice specifies the date by which the administrative penalty must be paid` AND `the notice sets out the brief details of the alleged contravention and such other particulars as may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contravention notice must — (a) specify the amount ...; (b) specify the date ...; and (c) set out the brief details"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5095 | (4) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice under
-- src:5096 | subsection (1) must pay the administrative penalty specified in the
-- src:5097 | contravention notice to the authorised officer within the time, in such
-- src:5098 | mode of payment and at such place as is specified in that notice.
@ref s 126B(4) (src:5095-5098)
GIVEN `the employer has been issued a contravention notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126B(4) the employer must pay the administrative penalty to the authorised officer` MEANS
    IF `the employer has been issued a contravention notice under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "any employer who is issued a contravention notice under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5095 | (4) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice under
-- src:5096 | subsection (1) must pay the administrative penalty specified in the
-- src:5097 | contravention notice to the authorised officer within the time, in such
-- src:5098 | mode of payment and at such place as is specified in that notice.
@ref s 126B(4) (src:5095-5098)
GIVEN `the day by which the notice requires the administrative penalty to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the day the administrative penalty is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126B(4) the payment is made within the time specified in the notice` MEANS
    IF `the day the administrative penalty is paid` AT MOST `the day by which the notice requires the administrative penalty to be paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must pay the administrative penalty specified in the contravention notice to the authorised officer within the time ... specified in that notice"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 126C Appeal, etc.`

-- src:5104 | 126C.—(1) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice by
-- src:5105 | an authorised officer under section 126B(1) (called in this section the
-- src:5106 | initial authorised officer) may —
-- src:5108 | (a) within the prescribed period and in accordance with the
-- src:5109 | prescribed procedure, request for an internal
-- src:5110 | reconsideration of the contravention notice by another
-- src:5111 | authorised officer (called in this section the reviewing
-- src:5112 | authorised officer); or
@ref s 126C(1)(a) (src:5104-5112)
GIVEN `the employer has been issued a contravention notice by an authorised officer under section 126B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made within the prescribed period and in accordance with the prescribed procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(1)(a) the employer may request an internal reconsideration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an employer issued a contravention notice
        IF NOT `the employer has been issued a contravention notice by an authorised officer under section 126B(1)` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the request is made within the prescribed period and in accordance with the prescribed procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the prescribed period and in accordance with the prescribed procedure, request for an internal reconsideration" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7): a request outside the prescribed period, or not in the prescribed procedure, is outside it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:5104 | 126C.—(1) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice by
-- src:5105 | an authorised officer under section 126B(1) (called in this section the
-- src:5106 | initial authorised officer) may —
-- src:5114 | (b) within the prescribed period (and despite not requesting for
-- src:5115 | an internal reconsideration), appeal to the General Division
-- src:5116 | of the High Court which may hear and determine the
-- src:5117 | matter afresh.
@ref s 126C(1)(b) (src:5104-5117)
GIVEN `the employer has been issued a contravention notice by an authorised officer under section 126B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(1)(b) the employer may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the employer has been issued a contravention notice by an authorised officer under section 126B(1)` THEN NOTHING
        -- "despite not requesting for an internal reconsideration"
        IF `the appeal is made within the prescribed period` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the prescribed period (and despite not requesting for an internal reconsideration), appeal to the General Division of the High Court" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7): an appeal outside the prescribed period is outside it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:5114 | (b) within the prescribed period (and despite not requesting for
-- src:5115 | an internal reconsideration), appeal to the General Division
-- src:5116 | of the High Court which may hear and determine the
-- src:5117 | matter afresh.
@ref s 126C(1)(b) (src:5114-5117)
GIVEN `an appeal has been filed under subsection (1)(b) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(1) the High Court may hear and determine the matter afresh` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been filed under subsection (1)(b) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the High Court "may hear and determine the matter afresh" on an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The prescribed period is in regulations that are not among the sources.  Its last day is an input; the three
-- steps (the request of (1)(a), the appeal of (1)(b), the appeal of (4)) are each "within the prescribed period".
-- src:5104 | 126C.—(1) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice by
-- src:5105 | an authorised officer under section 126B(1) (called in this section the
-- src:5106 | initial authorised officer) may —
-- src:5108 | (a) within the prescribed period and in accordance with the
-- src:5109 | prescribed procedure, request for an internal
-- src:5110 | reconsideration of the contravention notice by another
-- src:5111 | authorised officer (called in this section the reviewing
-- src:5112 | authorised officer); or
-- src:5114 | (b) within the prescribed period (and despite not requesting for
-- src:5115 | an internal reconsideration), appeal to the General Division
-- src:5116 | of the High Court which may hear and determine the
-- src:5117 | matter afresh.
@ref s 126C(1) (src:5104-5117)
GIVEN `the last day of the prescribed period` IS A DATE
      `the day the step is taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C the step is taken within the prescribed period` MEANS
    IF `the day the step is taken` AT MOST `the last day of the prescribed period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the prescribed period" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5121 | (2) A reviewing authorised officer reconsidering a contravention
-- src:5122 | notice issued to an employer must not be subordinate to the initial
-- src:5123 | authorised officer who issued the contravention notice.
@ref s 126C(2) (src:5121-5123)
GIVEN `the reviewing authorised officer is subordinate to the initial authorised officer who issued the contravention notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(2) the reviewing authorised officer is not barred from reconsidering the notice` MEANS
    IF `the reviewing authorised officer is subordinate to the initial authorised officer who issued the contravention notice`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reviewing authorised officer reconsidering a contravention notice issued to an employer must not be subordinate to the initial authorised officer"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 126C(3) Step after reconsidering` IS ONE OF
    `s 126C(3)(a) confirm the contravention notice issued by the initial authorised officer`
    `s 126C(3)(b) cancel the contravention notice`
    `s 126C(3) a step of some other kind`

-- src:5127 | (3) A reviewing authorised officer may, after reconsidering the
-- src:5128 | issue of a contravention notice by the initial authorised officer —
-- src:5130 | (a) confirm the contravention notice issued by the initial
-- src:5131 | authorised officer; or
-- src:5133 | (b) cancel the contravention notice.
@ref s 126C(3) (src:5127-5133)
GIVEN step IS A `s 126C(3) Step after reconsidering`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(3) the reviewing authorised officer may take the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER step
    WHEN `s 126C(3)(a) confirm the contravention notice issued by the initial authorised officer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 126C(3)(b) cancel the contravention notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (3) names two steps the reviewing officer may take and does not say the officer may take no other
    WHEN `s 126C(3) a step of some other kind` THEN NOTHING

-- src:5137 | (4) Any employer who is aggrieved by the reviewing authorised
-- src:5138 | officer’s decision under subsection (3)(a) may, within the prescribed
-- src:5143 | period, appeal to the General Division of the High Court which may
-- src:5144 | hear and determine the matter afresh.
@ref s 126C(4) (src:5137-5144)
GIVEN `the employer is aggrieved by the reviewing authorised officer's decision under subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(4) the employer may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an employer aggrieved by a decision to confirm
        IF NOT `the employer is aggrieved by the reviewing authorised officer's decision under subsection (3)(a)` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the appeal is made within the prescribed period` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within the prescribed period, appeal to the General Division of the High Court" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7): an appeal outside the prescribed period is outside it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:5148 | (5) The procedure governing any such appeal to the General
-- src:5149 | Division of the High Court is as provided in the Rules of Court.
@ref s 126C(5) (src:5148-5149)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an appeal to the General Division of the High Court under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(5) the procedure governing the appeal is as provided in the Rules of Court` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is an appeal to the General Division of the High Court under this section`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the procedure itself is in the Rules of Court, which are not in the text; TRUE here says only that the Rules of Court govern
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Fork F11: "until after the reconsideration is completed" and "until after the appeal is completed" are the end of the
-- stay; the encoding reads them as: stayed while the request or appeal is pending, and not stayed by this subsection otherwise
-- (JUST FALSE then: an unmet "if", or a bar that has run its course; rulings (b) and (d) of 2026-11-05).
-- src:5153 | (6) The enforcement of the payment of any administrative penalty
-- src:5154 | required by a contravention notice to be paid under section 126B is
-- src:5155 | stayed —
-- src:5157 | (a) if a request for internal reconsideration under
-- src:5158 | subsection (1)(a) is made, until after the reconsideration
-- src:5159 | is completed; or
-- src:5161 | (b) if an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) is filed, until
-- src:5162 | after the appeal is completed.
@ref s 126C(6) (src:5153-5162)
GIVEN `a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made and the reconsideration is not yet completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed and is not yet completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(6) the enforcement of the payment is stayed` MEANS
    IF `a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made and the reconsideration is not yet completed` OR `an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed and is not yet completed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) is made, until after the reconsideration is completed; or (b) if an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) is filed, until after the appeal is completed" (an unmet "if", ruling (b), and a bar whose "until after" has passed, ruling (d), 2026-11-05): with no request or appeal pending the subsection stays nothing
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Ruling (d), 2026-11-05: "stayed ... until after X" is a bar, asked as its own yes/no question (JUST TRUE until X, JUST FALSE
-- after X), and the thing the bar holds back is never said to have happened: the twin below is JUST FALSE while the bar
-- stands and NOTHING after it.
-- src:5153 | (6) The enforcement of the payment of any administrative penalty
-- src:5154 | required by a contravention notice to be paid under section 126B is
-- src:5155 | stayed —
-- src:5157 | (a) if a request for internal reconsideration under
-- src:5158 | subsection (1)(a) is made, until after the reconsideration
-- src:5159 | is completed; or
-- src:5161 | (b) if an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) is filed, until
-- src:5162 | after the appeal is completed.
@ref s 126C(6) (src:5153-5162)
GIVEN `a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reconsideration has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(6) the stay on the enforcement of the payment is still in force` MEANS
    IF (`a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made` AND NOT `the reconsideration has been completed`) OR (`an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed` AND NOT `the appeal has been completed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if a request ... is made, until after the reconsideration is completed; or (b) if an appeal ... is filed, until after the appeal is completed" (ruling (d), 2026-11-05): the bar ends once the reconsideration or appeal is completed, and does not begin when none is lodged
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5153 | (6) The enforcement of the payment of any administrative penalty
-- src:5154 | required by a contravention notice to be paid under section 126B is
-- src:5155 | stayed —
-- src:5157 | (a) if a request for internal reconsideration under
-- src:5158 | subsection (1)(a) is made, until after the reconsideration
-- src:5159 | is completed; or
-- src:5161 | (b) if an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) is filed, until
-- src:5162 | after the appeal is completed.
@ref s 126C(6) (src:5153-5162)
GIVEN `a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reconsideration has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(6) the enforcement of the payment is no longer held back and may go forward` MEANS
    IF (`a request for internal reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has been made` AND NOT `the reconsideration has been completed`) OR (`an appeal under subsection (1)(b) or (4) has been filed` AND NOT `the appeal has been completed`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "stayed ... until after the reconsideration is completed" and "until after the appeal is completed" (ruling (d), 2026-11-05): while either is pending the enforcement is held back
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (6) ends a stay; it does not say the payment may then be enforced, and subsection (7) lets a notice be enforced only by permission of a District Court
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5166 | (7) In relation to a contravention notice issued to an employer under
-- src:5167 | section 126B(1), where —
-- src:5169 | (a) an appeal to the General Division of the High Court has
-- src:5170 | been filed under subsection (1)(b) or (4) and the appeal is
-- src:5171 | dismissed;
-- src:5173 | (b) the prescribed period for requesting an internal
-- src:5174 | reconsideration under subsection (1)(a) has lapsed
-- src:5175 | without such request made, and the prescribed period for
-- src:5176 | filing an appeal to the General Division of the High Court
-- src:5177 | under subsection (1)(b) has lapsed and no appeal is filed; or
-- src:5179 | (c) the prescribed period for filing an appeal to the General
-- src:5180 | Division of the High Court under subsection (4) has lapsed
-- src:5181 | and no appeal is filed,
-- src:5183 | the contravention notice may, by permission of a District Court, be
-- src:5184 | enforced against the employer in the same manner as a judgment of
-- src:5185 | the District Court, and where permission is so given, judgment may
-- src:5186 | be entered in terms of that contravention notice.
@ref s 126C(7) (src:5166-5186)
GIVEN `an appeal has been filed under subsection (1)(b) or (4) and the appeal is dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed period for requesting an internal reconsideration has lapsed without a request, and the prescribed period for filing an appeal under subsection (1)(b) has lapsed and no appeal is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed period for filing an appeal under subsection (4) has lapsed and no appeal is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(7) the contravention notice may be enforced as a judgment of the District Court by its permission` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been filed under subsection (1)(b) or (4) and the appeal is dismissed` OR `the prescribed period for requesting an internal reconsideration has lapsed without a request, and the prescribed period for filing an appeal under subsection (1)(b) has lapsed and no appeal is filed` OR `the prescribed period for filing an appeal under subsection (4) has lapsed and no appeal is filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a contravention notice issued to an employer under section 126B(1), where — (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..., the contravention notice may, by permission of a District Court, be enforced" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): none of (a) to (c) holding, that route is not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5183 | the contravention notice may, by permission of a District Court, be
-- src:5184 | enforced against the employer in the same manner as a judgment of
-- src:5185 | the District Court, and where permission is so given, judgment may
-- src:5186 | be entered in terms of that contravention notice.
@ref s 126C(7) (src:5183-5186)
GIVEN `a District Court has given permission to enforce the contravention notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(7) judgment may be entered in terms of the contravention notice` MEANS
    IF `a District Court has given permission to enforce the contravention notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where permission is so given, judgment may be entered in terms of that contravention notice" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): without the District Court's permission it may not
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5195 | (8) The initial authorised officer may, in any case in which the
-- src:5196 | initial authorised officer thinks fit, waive, remit or refund in whole or
-- src:5197 | in part any administrative penalty paid or required to be paid under
-- src:5198 | section 126B.
@ref s 126C(8) (src:5195-5198)
GIVEN `the person is the initial authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial authorised officer thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126C(8) the initial authorised officer may waive, remit or refund the administrative penalty` MEANS
    IF `the person is the initial authorised officer` AND `the initial authorised officer thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of the initial authorised officer "in any case in which the initial authorised officer thinks fit"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 126D Directions`

-- src:5204 | 126D.—(1) In lieu of or in addition to giving an employer a
-- src:5205 | contravention notice under section 126B, an authorised officer
-- src:5206 | may —
-- src:5208 | (a) issue such directions to the employer as the authorised
-- src:5209 | officer thinks appropriate to bring the civil contravention
-- src:5210 | to an end; and
-- src:5212 | (b) where necessary, require the employer to take such action
-- src:5213 | as is specified in the direction to remedy, mitigate or
-- src:5214 | eliminate any effects of the civil contravention and to
-- src:5215 | prevent the recurrence of the civil contravention.
@ref s 126D(1) (src:5204-5215)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 126A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126D(1) the authorised officer may give the direction` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authorised officer` AND `the answer of s 126A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an authorised officer, "in lieu of or in addition to giving an employer a contravention notice", about a civil contravention
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (b): "where necessary, require the employer to take such action as is specified in the direction" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05).
-- src:5212 | (b) where necessary, require the employer to take such action
-- src:5213 | as is specified in the direction to remedy, mitigate or
-- src:5214 | eliminate any effects of the civil contravention and to
-- src:5215 | prevent the recurrence of the civil contravention.
@ref s 126D(1)(b) (src:5212-5215)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 126A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to require the employer to take the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126D(1)(b) the authorised officer may require the employer to take the action specified in the direction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where necessary, require the employer to take such action as is specified in the direction to remedy, mitigate or eliminate any effects of the civil contravention and to prevent the recurrence of the civil contravention" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): where it is not necessary the power is not given
        IF NOT `it is necessary to require the employer to take the action` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the person is an authorised officer` AND `the answer of s 126A` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of an authorised officer, about a civil contravention (ruling (c), 2026-11-05)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5219 | (2) An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply
-- src:5220 | with a direction given to the employer under subsection (1) shall be
-- src:5221 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:5222 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:5223 | 6 months or to both.
@ref s 126D(2) (src:5219-5223)
GIVEN `a direction has been given to the employer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126D(2) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of an employer who fails to comply with a direction given under subsection (1)
        IF NOT (`a direction has been given to the employer under subsection (1)` AND `the employer has failed to comply with the direction`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the employer has a reasonable excuse` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a direction ... shall be guilty of an offence" is limited by "without reasonable excuse" and does not say that an employer with a reasonable excuse is not guilty (marginal reading (b); the other reading answers JUST FALSE)
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5219 | (2) An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply
-- src:5220 | with a direction given to the employer under subsection (1) shall be
-- src:5221 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:5222 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:5223 | 6 months or to both.
@ref s 126D(2) (src:5219-5223)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 126D(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH
                   `least fine in dollars` IS 0
                   `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
                   `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is of an employer "liable on conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5219 | (2) An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply
-- src:5220 | with a direction given to the employer under subsection (1) shall be
-- src:5221 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:5222 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:5223 | 6 months or to both.
@ref s 126D(2) (src:5219-5223)
GIVEN `the employer is convicted of the offence under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126D(2) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the employer is convicted of the offence under subsection (2)`
    -- "or to both"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the fine, the imprisonment or both are for an employer liable on conviction
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 15A -- the duties and permissions as regulative rules`

DECLARE `Part 15A Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 126B(4) the employer`
    `s 126C(1) the employer`
    `s 126D(2) the employer`

DECLARE `Part 15A Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 126B(4) pay the administrative penalty to the authorised officer`
    `s 126C(1) request a reconsideration or appeal`
    `s 126D(2) comply with the direction`

-- src:5095 | (4) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice under
-- src:5096 | subsection (1) must pay the administrative penalty specified in the
-- src:5097 | contravention notice to the authorised officer within the time, in such
-- src:5098 | mode of payment and at such place as is specified in that notice.
@ref s 126B(4) (src:5095-5098)
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part 15A Party` `Part 15A Act`
`s 126B(4) rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 126B(4) the employer`
    MUST `s 126B(4) pay the administrative penalty to the authorised officer`
    WITHIN days
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

-- src:5104 | 126C.—(1) Any employer who is issued a contravention notice by
-- src:5105 | an authorised officer under section 126B(1) (called in this section the
-- src:5106 | initial authorised officer) may —
-- src:5108 | (a) within the prescribed period and in accordance with the
-- src:5109 | prescribed procedure, request for an internal
-- src:5110 | reconsideration of the contravention notice by another
-- src:5111 | authorised officer (called in this section the reviewing
-- src:5112 | authorised officer); or
-- src:5114 | (b) within the prescribed period (and despite not requesting for
-- src:5115 | an internal reconsideration), appeal to the General Division
-- src:5116 | of the High Court which may hear and determine the
-- src:5117 | matter afresh.
@ref s 126C(1) (src:5104-5117)
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part 15A Party` `Part 15A Act`
`s 126C(1) rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 126C(1) the employer`
    MAY `s 126C(1) request a reconsideration or appeal`
    WITHIN days
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:5219 | (2) An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply
-- src:5220 | with a direction given to the employer under subsection (1) shall be
-- src:5221 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:5222 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:5223 | 6 months or to both.
@ref s 126D(2) (src:5219-5223)
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part 15A Party` `Part 15A Act`
`s 126D(2) rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 126D(2) the employer`
    MUST `s 126D(2) comply with the direction`
    WITHIN days
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE (`s 126B(4) rule` 30) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 126B(4) the employer` DOES `s 126B(4) pay the administrative penalty to the authorised officer` AT 30

#TRACE (`s 126B(4) rule` 30) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 126B(4) the employer` DOES `s 126B(4) pay the administrative penalty to the authorised officer` AT 31

#TRACE (`s 126C(1) rule` 14) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 126C(1) the employer` DOES `s 126C(1) request a reconsideration or appeal` AT 14

#TRACE (`s 126D(2) rule` 7) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 126D(2) the employer` DOES `s 126D(2) comply with the direction` AT 7

#TRACE (`s 126D(2) rule` 7) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 126D(2) the employer` DOES `s 126D(2) comply with the direction` AT 8
